\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The inflating throat ($\varepsilon =-10^{-2}$; $L=512$, level 5) to $t=218$. (a)~Neck areal radius in the full metric, $3.81\to 14.5$; gold, the exponential onset, $T=5.7$ over $t=16$--$28$; shaded, the Shinkai--Hayward rate ($t=16$--$40$, gold) and the slower growth in $t$ once $1{+}\log $ freezes the neck's clock (grey). (b)~Over that window the neck's proper-time rate is $HR_0=1.22$ (local $1.0$--$1.3$), against Shinkai--Hayward's massless $Ha=1.1$ and the linear mode's $1.30$. (c)~The $\theta _l=0$ horizon stays on the neck; $\theta _k=0$ runs out to $R\approx 73$ by $t=212$. (d)~The lapse at the neck falls $0.57\to 0.015$; dashed, its minimum on the finest box. (e),(f)~$\max |K|$ and $\min \chi $ on the finest box, around the origin. (g),(h)~$\chi $ and $\alpha $ per shell (light = early): the $\chi $ peak moves out with the neck. Constraint norms: Fig.~\ref {fig:constraints}(d). The throat keeps growing, anti-trapped; its onset is at the linear rate.}}{8}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:single_inflation}{{3}{8}{The inflating throat ($\varepsilon =-10^{-2}$; $L=\clmFourBoxL $, level \clmFourLevel ) to $t=\clmFourWall $. (a)~Neck areal radius in the full metric, $\clmFourRStart \to \clmFourRWall $; gold, the exponential onset, $T=\clmFourOnsetEfold $ over $t=\clmFourOnsetLo $--$\clmFourOnsetHi $; shaded, the Shinkai--Hayward rate ($t=\clmFourSHWinLo $--$\clmFourSHWinHi $, gold) and the slower growth in $t$ once $1{+}\log $ freezes the neck's clock (grey). (b)~Over that window the neck's proper-time rate is $HR_0=\clmFourSHRate $ (local $\clmFourSHLocalLo $--$\clmFourSHLocalHi $), against Shinkai--Hayward's massless $Ha=\clmSHMassless $ and the linear mode's $\clmFourLinearRate $. (c)~The $\theta _l=0$ horizon stays on the neck; $\theta _k=0$ runs out to $R\approx \clmFourHorizonR $ by $t=\clmFourHorizonTime $. (d)~The lapse at the neck falls $\clmFourLapseStart \to \clmFourLapseEnd $; dashed, its minimum on the finest box. (e),(f)~$\max |K|$ and $\min \chi $ on the finest box, around the origin. (g),(h)~$\chi $ and $\alpha $ per shell (light = early): the $\chi $ peak moves out with the neck. Constraint norms: Fig.~\ref {fig:constraints}(d). The throat keeps growing, anti-trapped; its onset is at the linear rate}{figure.3}{}}
