\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The production spiral ($p=0.12$, $d=12$, $L=128$) as one history: level 3 to $t=36$, level 5 to the wall at $t=60.45$ (cross), and the frozen-core leg (shaded: $r\le 1.9$ frozen from $t=57$, live exterior to $t=100$), from which no core quantity is drawn. Rules: the level $3\to 5$ handover (solid), the merger transient at $t=41.2$ (dashed) and $\chi $ on its floor from $t=58.4$ (dotted). (a)~Coordinate separation of the two $\chi $ pits, each a wormhole's compactified far side, pale once $\chi $ is floored; gold diamonds mark the slices carrying a common MOTS. (b)~Areal radius $R=\sqrt  {A/4\pi }$ of the common MOTS (gold diamonds: filled, this chain; open, the arm evolved at level 5 from $t=0$) and of the common neck, the smallest coordinate sphere about the pits' midpoint (circles: open, level 3; filled, level 5), against one initial throat ($R_\star $) and the radius $\sqrt  2R_\star $ of the two throats' summed area. (c)~Core extrema; $\max |K|$ dash-dotted. (d)~Coordinate radius of the $|K|$ peak (from $t=49.1$, before which the profile is flat), of its $|K|>0.2$ edge (dashed) and of the neck (circles). Constraint norms: Fig.~\ref {fig:constraints}(f).}}{12}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:spiral_collapse}{{6}{12}{The production spiral ($p=\clmSpiralMomentumProd $, $d=12$, $L=128$) as one history: level 3 to $t=\clmSpiralRestartTime $, level 5 to the wall at $t=\clmSpiralDeath $ (cross), and the frozen-core leg (shaded: $r\le \clmSpiralFillRadius $ frozen from $t=\clmGwFreezeStart $, live exterior to $t=\clmFreezeEnd $), from which no core quantity is drawn. Rules: the level $3\to 5$ handover (solid), the merger transient at $t=\clmSpiralTransientTime $ (dashed) and $\chi $ on its floor from $t=\clmSpiralChiFloorTime $ (dotted). (a)~Coordinate separation of the two $\chi $ pits, each a wormhole's compactified far side, pale once $\chi $ is floored; gold diamonds mark the slices carrying a common MOTS. (b)~Areal radius $R=\sqrt {A/4\pi }$ of the common MOTS (gold diamonds: filled, this chain; open, the arm evolved at level 5 from $t=0$) and of the common neck, the smallest coordinate sphere about the pits' midpoint (circles: open, level 3; filled, level 5), against one initial throat ($R_\star $) and the radius $\sqrt 2R_\star $ of the two throats' summed area. (c)~Core extrema; $\max |K|$ dash-dotted. (d)~Coordinate radius of the $|K|$ peak (from $t=\clmSpiralSpikeStart $, before which the profile is flat), of its $|K|>\clmSpiralEdgeThreshold $ edge (dashed) and of the neck (circles). Constraint norms: Fig.~\ref {fig:constraints}(f)}{figure.6}{}}
