\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Every source at one calibration: total mass $30\,M_\odot $ at $10$ Mpc, each record in units of its own total ADM mass. (a)~Envelopes $|r\Psi _4|M$ at the innermost sphere, aligned at each peak: fly-by loudest ($8.2\times 10^{-2}$) to lone throat ($3.1\times 10^{-3}$). (b)~Strain amplitude spectral densities over the aLIGO design floor (gold), each from its own low-frequency corner (one cycle per record, ticked). The curves are falling power laws (slopes $-3.4$ to $-5.8$) with no resolved maximum, so any ``peak'' read here is the corner $1/T$. Faint line: the Newtonian inspiral of the same binary, $|\tilde  h|\propto f^{-7/6}$ to its ISCO at $147$ Hz. (c)~Instantaneous frequency against the point-mass chirp (gold), the ISCO ($147$ Hz) and the equal-mass Kerr ringdown ($599$ Hz): the vacuum twin climbs the chirp and peaks at $fM=0.065$; no wormhole channel does (Sec.~\ref {sec:ligo:ringdown}). (d)~Energy radiated in the dominant multipole; ticks give the spread over spheres (fly-by $43\%$, the widest). Open gold bars: published equal-mass vacuum values from rest at infinity---head-on infall $5.5\times 10^{-4}$, quasi-circular merger $4.84\times 10^{-2}$. Energies are band integrals of $|\DOTSI \intop \ilimits@ r\Psi _4\,\mathrm  {d}t'|^2$ over a common retarded window, doubled for $\pm m$; gravitational channel only. At $10^{4}$--$10^{6}\,M_\odot $ and $z_e\simeq 20$ the same records are millihertz LISA sources (Sec.~\ref {sec:discussion:seeds}, Fig.~\ref {fig:heavy_seeds}).}}{15}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gw_ligo}{{8}{15}{Every source at one calibration: total mass $\clmGwLigoMass \,M_\odot $ at $\clmGwLigoDist $ Mpc, each record in units of its own total ADM mass. (a)~Envelopes $|r\Psi _4|M$ at the innermost sphere, aligned at each peak: fly-by loudest ($\clmGwEnvPeakFlyby $) to lone throat ($\clmGwEnvPeakThroat $). (b)~Strain amplitude spectral densities over the aLIGO design floor (gold), each from its own low-frequency corner (one cycle per record, ticked). The curves are falling power laws (slopes $\clmGwSlopeShallow $ to $\clmGwSlopeSteep $) with no resolved maximum, so any ``peak'' read here is the corner $1/T$. Faint line: the Newtonian inspiral of the same binary, $|\tilde h|\propto f^{-7/6}$ to its ISCO at $\clmGwIscoHz $ Hz. (c)~Instantaneous frequency against the point-mass chirp (gold), the ISCO ($\clmGwIscoHz $ Hz) and the equal-mass Kerr ringdown ($\clmGwKerrHz $ Hz): the vacuum twin climbs the chirp and peaks at $fM=\clmGwTwinPeakFM $; no wormhole channel does (Sec.~\ref {sec:ligo:ringdown}). (d)~Energy radiated in the dominant multipole; ticks give the spread over spheres (fly-by $\clmGwSpreadFlyby \%$, the widest). Open gold bars: published equal-mass vacuum values from rest at infinity---head-on infall $\clmGwLitHeadonInfall $, quasi-circular merger $\clmGwLitCircular $. Energies are band integrals of $|\int r\Psi _4\,\mathrm {d}t'|^2$ over a common retarded window, doubled for $\pm m$; gravitational channel only. At $\clmDetSeedMassLo $--$\clmDetSeedMassHi \,M_\odot $ and $z_e\simeq \clmDetZConv $ the same records are millihertz LISA sources (Sec.~\ref {sec:discussion:seeds}, Fig.~\ref {fig:heavy_seeds})}{figure.8}{}}
