\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces The heavy-seed channel from measured numbers. (a)~Seed growth: a drainhole population of $10^{4}$--$10^{6}\,M_\odot $ converts at birth ($z\simeq 20$, seconds to minutes; Table~\ref {tab:scales}), so its reachable region (gold) runs from the lightest seed idling to the heaviest seed's Eddington ceiling (Salpeter e-fold $45$ Myr). UHZ1~\cite  {bogdan2024,natarajan2024}, GN-z11~\cite  {maiolino2024}, the $z=7.5$ quasar J1342$+$0928~\cite  {banados2018} and the little-red-dot box~\cite  {greene2024,matthee2024} lie inside it; the first three lie \emph  {above} the ceiling of a $10^{2}\,M_\odot $ light seed started at $z=25$ (grey), which misses UHZ1 by two{} decades. (b)~One burst against LISA: the characteristic strain $h_c=2f|\tilde  h|$ of a fly-by (gold) at each mass decade from $10^{4}$ to $10^{8}\,M_\odot $ (exponents at the tracks), and of a spiral (blue) and a lone collapse (grey) at $10^{5}\,M_\odot $, all at $z_e=20$, against $\sqrt  {fS_n}$ of the analytic LISA noise~\cite  {robson2019} with the four-year galactic confusion (ink); inclination averaged, each track drawn over the band holding $90\%$ of its $\DOTSI \intop \ilimits@ h_c^2\,\mathrm  {d}\ln f$; the $10^{7}\,M_\odot $ fly-by's counted signal lies in its tail above the band floor, past the drawn core. The squared ratio of track to noise, integrated over $\ln f$, is the burst's squared signal-to-noise ratio, so a short track can sit above the noise and still fall short of 8, as the lone collapse does. Heavier bursts are louder but redder: the tracks climb a decade per mass decade, the noise climbs faster below $0.1$ mHz (hatched: below LISA's band, not counted), and the $10^{8}\,M_\odot $ burst lies wholly below it. At the abundances of (c) the population is ${\sim }0.05$--$5$ resolved bursts per year (Sec.~\ref {sec:discussion:seeds}). (c)~$\Omega _{\rm  GW}$ of the conversions (gold, $E/M$ from the head-on to the spiral) and the negative scalar deposit $|\Omega _{\phi ,0}|$ (blue, $|E_\phi |=0.8$--$3.2\,E_{\rm  GW}$ with $E_{\rm  GW}$ from the spiral to the fly-by: every encounter, the case most favourable to $\Lambda $) today against the comoving mass density $nM$ of converting wormholes, on which alone both depend (top axis: $\Omega _{\rm  WH}=nM/\rho _c$). Solid up to the dark-matter ceiling $nM=\rho _{\rm  DM}$ (vertical rule), faint beyond it: $\Omega _\Lambda $ is reached only at $\Omega _{\rm  WH}\simeq 60$--$800$, above the cap $|\rho _\phi |=\rho _m$ at $z_e$ that $H^2>0$ imposes (dashed). Ink ticks: the four-year power-law-integrated LISA sensitivity~\cite  {thrane2013} at each mass's conversion frequency $(fM)_{\rm  peak}/[M(1+z_e)]$. Grey: one seed per little red dot~\cite  {greene2024,matthee2024} at $10^{4}$--$10^{6}\,M_\odot $.}}{18}{figure.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:heavy_seeds}{{9}{18}{The heavy-seed channel from measured numbers. (a)~Seed growth: a drainhole population of $\clmDetSeedMassLo $--$\clmDetSeedMassHi \,M_\odot $ converts at birth ($z\simeq \clmDetZConv $, seconds to minutes; Table~\ref {tab:scales}), so its reachable region (gold) runs from the lightest seed idling to the heaviest seed's Eddington ceiling (Salpeter e-fold $\clmDetSalpeter $ Myr). UHZ1~\cite {bogdan2024,natarajan2024}, GN-z11~\cite {maiolino2024}, the $z=\clmDetJQuasarZ $ quasar J1342$+$0928~\cite {banados2018} and the little-red-dot box~\cite {greene2024,matthee2024} lie inside it; the first three lie \emph {above} the ceiling of a $\clmDetLightSeedMass \,M_\odot $ light seed started at $z=\clmDetLightSeedZ $ (grey), which misses UHZ1 by \clmDetLightSeedGap {} decades. (b)~One burst against LISA: the characteristic strain $h_c=2f|\tilde h|$ of a fly-by (gold) at each mass decade from $\clmDetSeedMassLo $ to $\clmDetConvMassHi \,M_\odot $ (exponents at the tracks), and of a spiral (blue) and a lone collapse (grey) at $\clmDetSeedMassMid \,M_\odot $, all at $z_e=\clmDetZConv $, against $\sqrt {fS_n}$ of the analytic LISA noise~\cite {robson2019} with the four-year galactic confusion (ink); inclination averaged, each track drawn over the band holding $\clmDetTrackShare \%$ of its $\int h_c^2\,\mathrm {d}\ln f$; the $\clmDetConvMassLo \,M_\odot $ fly-by's counted signal lies in its tail above the band floor, past the drawn core. The squared ratio of track to noise, integrated over $\ln f$, is the burst's squared signal-to-noise ratio, so a short track can sit above the noise and still fall short of 8, as the lone collapse does. Heavier bursts are louder but redder: the tracks climb a decade per mass decade, the noise climbs faster below $\clmDetBandFloor $ mHz (hatched: below LISA's band, not counted), and the $\clmDetConvMassHi \,M_\odot $ burst lies wholly below it. At the abundances of (c) the population is ${\sim }\clmDetRateLo $--$\clmDetRateHi $ resolved bursts per year (Sec.~\ref {sec:discussion:seeds}). (c)~$\Omega _{\rm GW}$ of the conversions (gold, $E/M$ from the head-on to the spiral) and the negative scalar deposit $|\Omega _{\phi ,0}|$ (blue, $|E_\phi |=\clmGwScalarRatioEighty $--$\clmGwScalarRatioFifty \,E_{\rm GW}$ with $E_{\rm GW}$ from the spiral to the fly-by: every encounter, the case most favourable to $\Lambda $) today against the comoving mass density $nM$ of converting wormholes, on which alone both depend (top axis: $\Omega _{\rm WH}=nM/\rho _c$). Solid up to the dark-matter ceiling $nM=\rho _{\rm DM}$ (vertical rule), faint beyond it: $\Omega _\Lambda $ is reached only at $\Omega _{\rm WH}\simeq \clmDetOmegaWHLo $--$\clmDetOmegaWHHi $, above the cap $|\rho _\phi |=\rho _m$ at $z_e$ that $H^2>0$ imposes (dashed). Ink ticks: the four-year power-law-integrated LISA sensitivity~\cite {thrane2013} at each mass's conversion frequency $(fM)_{\rm peak}/[M(1+z_e)]$. Grey: one seed per little red dot~\cite {greene2024,matthee2024} at $\clmDetSeedMassLo $--$\clmDetSeedMassHi \,M_\odot $}{figure.9}{}}
